      <data key="d7">Aldicarb metabolism in topsoil is thought to occur mainly through microbial activity.</data>
      <data key="d8">descriptive</data>
      <data key="d9">{"crop_or_species": "", "population": "", "condition": "in topsoil", "comparator": "", "metric": ""}</data>
      <data key="d10">False</data>
      <data key="d11">Integrated Soil and Crop Management in Organic Agriculture: A Logical Framework to Ensure Food Quality and Human Health?</data>
      <data key="d12">Soil-applied herbicides and insecticides are known to be absorbed by soil organic matter, and aldicarb metabolism in topsoil is thought to be mainly by microbial activity [144,145], which is known to be higher in soils receiving regular organic fertilizer inputs [78,146–148].</data>
